ne @zenglingbiao @zhangguiping-xydt @zhuyankarl @zwyhmcn @zyw02\n\n### Release verification\n\n- Signed source: `3a9d69db306cd7f081e06254cb89c4bcc14a7107`.\n- [Full stable validation](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/34539227282): passed, attempt 2. Qualification also verified 15 performance measurements and 20 real OpenAI completions across 10 upgrade baselines.\n- [Core npm publication](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/34554632555): passed; exact qualified bytes, registry signatures, provenance and fresh install verified.\n- 90 npm plugins and 3 core companion packages: published at `latest`, exact bytes verified.\n- [Docker publication](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/34555843439): passed; public GHCR and Docker Hub manifests and attestations match qualified artifacts.\n- [Original publisher](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/34552806250): failed during npm propagation readback. GitHub finalized through manual recovery; no package republish.\n- Telegram and Parallels checks: explicitly waived by the release owner, not passed.\n- macOS DMG, ZIP, and debug symbols are public and byte-verified against the signed/notarized artifacts; the [stable update feed](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/144636) is live and verified.\n- Pending: ClawHub recovery, npm beta-selector synchronization, remaining native app distribution, and stable main closeout. Android native qualification failed. Windows historical-upgrade and Vercel mirror advisory failures remain recorded.\n- The [repaired split-publication verifier](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/144638) passed live npm/Docker verification. Full beta-selector verification and the immutable main-closeout record remain pending. The attached postpublish evidence preserves the earlier recovery snapshot; these follow-ups are not marked complete.\n- Linux desktop AppImage and Debian package: published from `v2026.9.4` source `3a9d69db306cd7f081e06254cb89c4bcc14a7107`. [Build, packaged runtime smoke, and signing](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/34749148773) passed; GitHub asset upload was recovered using the exact successful CI artifacts. Public downloads match the [checksums](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases/download/v2026.9.4/SHA256SUMS.linux-app.txt), and the AppImage signature was independently verified. The [Linux updater manifest](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/releases/download/v2026.9.4/latest.json) is published, and the stable update endpoint was verified at 2026.9.4.\n",
